# /usr/vellum/frag - the shop's FRAGMENT library (VELLUM.md sec. 50).
#
# A fragment is a DRAWING.  There is no fragment format, no fragment
# index and no fragment code: a shop-standard detail is a .d file in
# this directory, its index is `ls', and it reaches the editor the way
# any other drawing text does -- through the PRIMARY selection:
#
#	hrclip < /usr/vellum/frag/legend.d
#
# from any shell puts it on the selection; a MIDDLE CLICK in the editor
# pastes it at the pointer, because dopaste has parsed .d text out of
# the selection since v1.3.  Copy this directory, add your own, delete
# ours: it is a directory of drawings, and that is all it is.
